# CVEs accepted in the upstream quay.io/keycloak/keycloak image (libraries bundled by Keycloak itself, not by
# this project). Remove each entry once a Keycloak release ships the fixed library (Dependabot tracks the base image).
# Reviewed 2026-09-24 against Keycloak 26.7.4.

# netty-handler 4.1.136 (fixed in 4.1.137): SNI routing bypass. Not reachable: TLS terminates at nginx and
# Keycloak only serves plain HTTP on the loopback interface.
CVE-2026-75595

# bcprov-jdk18on 1.84 (fixed in 1.85): X.509 Name Constraints bypass. Only affects certificate path validation
# (mTLS / X.509 client authentication), which is not used.
CVE-2026-8763

# bcprov-jdk18on 1.84 (fixed in 1.85): denial of service via lazy ASN.1 sequence parsing.
CVE-2026-13506

# mssql-jdbc 13.2.1: false positive, 13.2.1 is itself listed as a fixed version; the SQL Server driver is not used
# (the image is built for PostgreSQL).
CVE-2025-59250

# pcre2 / pcre2-syntax 10.40-6.el9 (OS package of the UBI 9 base image, not a Keycloak library). No fixed version.
# Exploiting either one requires a program that uses PCRE2 to compile or run an attacker-chosen regular expression;
# Keycloak runs on the JVM and uses java.util.regex, and PCRE2 is only there for base-image system utilities.
# Not reported by this repo's CI (ignore-unfixed) but listed by the weekly unfiltered scan of the deployed image
# (gointerop/gointerop-keycloak cve-scan.yaml, run 36018713095). Accepted on 2026-09-24.
# CVE-2026-86145: out-of-bounds write via crafted regular expression. Red Hat status: will_not_fix, so it stays
# for as long as Keycloak ships on UBI 9.
CVE-2026-86145
# CVE-2026-89161: memory corruption in pcre2_jit_match. Red Hat status: affected (fix not published yet).
CVE-2026-89161
